      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## **10. Comparing Word Embeddings**\n",
        "\n",
        "**How can you visualize weight similarity?**\n",
        "\n",
        "For an input word, the weights leaving it towards the hidden neurons form the corresponding **row of `weights_0_1`**. Each entry of that row is the weight from the word to one hidden neuron. To find the words most similar to a target word, each word's vector (its row) is compared with the vector of the target. The comparison used is the **Euclidean distance**. The function `similar` computes the negative of this distance for every word of the vocabulary (so that the most similar words have the highest scores) and returns the ten best ones."
      ],
      "id": "c11-s10"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c11-code-similar-def"
